            <fr:title text="Polarizations and the trace-form generators">Polarizations and the trace-form generators</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For commuting indeterminates <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[s, t]]></fr:tex> and two generic matrices
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X, Y]]></fr:tex>, the <html:em>polarizations</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P_{a,b}]]></fr:tex> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_{j}]]></fr:tex> are
defined by <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  c_{j}(sX + tY) = \sum _{a + b = j} s^a t^b P_{a,b}(X, Y),
]]></fr:tex>
bihomogeneous of bidegree <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(a, b)]]></fr:tex>, with
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P_{j,0} = c_{j}(X)]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[P_{0,j} = c_{j}(Y)]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[j \le  4]]></fr:tex> these are explicit combinations of twisted trace
forms <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {tr}(X^{a_1} F(X)^{b_1} \cdots  X^{a_r} F(X)^{b_r})
]]></fr:tex>
— the sparse trace-form generators. Setting <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Y = F(X)]]></fr:tex> recovers the
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod powers</fr:link>, by
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">the evaluation identity</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">Setup: conjugation over a finite field</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The q-Steenrod operations</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">The evaluation identity</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal sec:polarization.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0005</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0005/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The Steenrod ideal">The Steenrod ideal</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  J \coloneqq  \bigl ( \mathcal {P}^{i}(c_{j}) : 1 \le  j \le  n,
  0 \le  i \le  j-1 \bigr ) \subseteq  S,
]]></fr:tex>
an ideal generated by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {n+1}{2} = \frac {n(n+1)}{2}]]></fr:tex> invariants, of
degrees <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[j + i(q-1)]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>By the vanishing facts of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod operations</fr:link>
the omitted Steenrod powers contribute nothing, so <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[V(J)]]></fr:tex> is
the common zero locus of <html:em>all</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}^{i}(c_{j})]]></fr:tex>,
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i \ge  0]]></fr:tex>. For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 2]]></fr:tex> the ideal is exactly Maithani's primary ideal
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(\operatorname {tr}, \det , \mathcal {P}^{1}(\det ))]]></fr:tex> up to the orbit product.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">Setup: conjugation over a finite field</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The q-Steenrod operations</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0004/" title="Polarizations and the trace-form generators" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0004/" display-uri="ffi-0004" type="local">Polarizations and the trace-form generators</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: Maithani 2025 for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 2]]></fr:tex>; journal sec:ideal.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0003</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0003/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The evaluation identity">The evaluation identity</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f \in  S]]></fr:tex> and every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M \in  \mathrm {M}_n(K)]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \sum _{i \ge  0} \mathcal {P}^{i}(f)(M) T^i = f(M + T F(M))
  \qquad  \text {in } K[T].
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}]]></fr:tex> is a substitution homomorphism, so it commutes with
evaluation. This one line is what the whole height program runs on:
<html:em>Steenrod operations are deformation calculus in the Frobenius
direction</html:em>. Every subsequent statement about <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[V(J)]]></fr:tex> — the
pencil criterion, the flag witnesses — is read off it.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">Setup: conjugation over a finite field</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The q-Steenrod operations</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: distilled.tex Part 1; journal sec:steenrod.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sec-foundations</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest › Foundations"><fr:link href="/ffi/index/" title="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/index/" display-uri="index" type="local">finite-field-invariants: a reference forest</fr:link> › Foundations</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>From the conjugation action to the statement of the height
  conjecture.</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">The setup</fr:link> — the action, the characteristic
    polynomial, Frobenius.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod operations</fr:link> — the operations, and
    what they do to degrees.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">The evaluation identity</fr:link> — the one fact the program
    runs on.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0004/" title="Polarizations and the trace-form generators" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0004/" display-uri="ffi-0004" type="local">The polarizations</fr:link> — the sparse trace-form
    generators.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link> — the ideal whose height is in
    question.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0006/" title="The pencil criterion" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0006/" display-uri="ffi-0006" type="local">The pencil criterion</fr:link> — nilpotency to all orders in
    the Frobenius direction.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0007/" title="Flag witnesses for the partner variety" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0007/" display-uri="ffi-0007" type="local">The flag witnesses</fr:link> — the subvarieties that attain
    the lower bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0008/" title="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0008/" display-uri="ffi-0008" type="local">The Krull bound</fr:link> — why the whole question is an upper
    bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> — the conjecture itself.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> — what is actually left to prove.</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
